{{See also|Pay-to-play Crafting training}}
This [[Skill training guides|guide]] outlines the best methods and alternative options for training the [[Crafting]] [[skill]] in [[free-to-play]].


==Quests that reward Crafting experience==
*[[Sheep Shearer]]: 150 Crafting experience
*[[Goblin Diplomacy]]: 200 Crafting experience
*[[Misthalin Mystery]]: 600 Crafting experience

Completing all of these quests will provide enough experience to level up Crafting from level 1 to level 8.

==Potter's wheel, spinning wheel and furnace locations==
[[Barbarian Village]] has a [[potter's wheel]] medium distance to closest bank (West [[Varrock]] bank). No clay rocks or water source nearby. 

* Varrock south-west mine to Varrock west bank is a good place to mine clay.
* [[Waterpump (Falador)]] to Falador west bank is the closest water source to a bank. Water fountain in centre of Varrock square to Varrock west bank is also a good water source close to a bank.

Lumbridge bank to the [[spinning wheel]] downstairs is a good combination for a bank plus spinning wheel.

[[Edgeville]] has the [[furnace]] closest to a bank for crafting silver or gold. Al Kharid bank to a furnace is a decent location for a relatively short distance between bank and furnace, for crafting silver and gold.

Upon reaching Crafting Level 40, the [[Crafting Guild]] has no bank nearby, but contains clay rocks, a water source , a potter's wheel, and a pottery kiln. The crafting guild also has  two [[spinning wheel]]s. A flock of wool-producing sheep can be found just a short walk north of the guild.
===Ultimate Ironman===
At level 23 Crafting and with 20 Mining and Smithing, [[ultimate ironmen]] can mine [[silver ore]] at the [[Al Kharid mine|Al Karid Mine]], teleport to the [[Lumbridge cow field]] using the [[Cowbell amulet|Cowbell Amulet]] and then craft [[Tiara|tiaras]] at the [[Lumbridge]] furnace. Players can then sell tiaras to the Lumbridge General store for a modest profit, and walk back to the mine. This method can yield 1409 exp per run with 27 open inventory slots.   

Until level 40, [[ultimate ironmen]] can mine clay in [[West Varrock mine]], then walk to the water fountain and fill up buckets of water to turn clay into soft clay. Then return to Barbarian Village wheel and kiln, then boat back down to [[Champions' Guild]]/West Varrock mine. Yields 650–720 experience per run, depending on the amount of open inventory spaces.

After level 40, use the Crafting Guild. Mining and smelting gold, crafting them into jewellery to sell at [[Grum's Gold Exchange.]] is a good way to make money while training [[Mining]], Crafting and [[Smithing]] as an Ultimate Ironman.<!-- At what furnace? This advice is wrong -->

